{
  "_comment": "USD per 1M tokens, from each provider's published price list. gpt-4.1 and gpt-4.1-mini are here for the search transport (they support web_search; gpt-5-nano does not). Anthropic rows checked against platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing, ids and max_output against the live Models API: cache_write is the 1-hour TTL price (2x input; the engine caches with ttl=1h), cached_input is 0.1x input except Opus 5.5 / Sonnet 5.5 (0.05x) and Fable 5.1 (0.025x); Sonnet 5 is $2/$10 (the introductory price became standard); Haiku 5.5 is the rate for prompts up to 100,000 tokens ($0.50/$2.50 above). cache_min_tokens for Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5 is unpublished and set to 1024 provisionally (Haiku 5.5 has cached a longer prefix live). Prices and model IDs change often - re-verify before relying on cost estimates. cache_min_tokens is the shortest prefix that will cache; shorter prefixes silently do not cache. DeepSeek rates are OFF-PEAK; peak (01:00-04:00 and 06:00-10:00 UTC, Mon-Fri) is roughly double.",
  "_schema": {
    "input": "standard input price",
    "cached_input": "price for a prefix served from cache",
    "cache_write": "price to write a cache entry (null = no separate charge)",
    "output": "output price",
    "batch_discount": "multiplier applied to all token prices in batch mode",
    "cache_min_tokens": "minimum cacheable prefix length",
    "context": "context window in tokens",
    "max_output": "output cap in tokens; max_tokens above it is rejected (optional, recorded for Anthropic)",
    "effort": "false when the model takes no effort setting (not a reasoning model, or one the API refuses effort on): the engine then sends none (optional; absent means the provider's rule applies)",
    "effort_levels": "the effort levels this model takes where they differ from its provider's (optional; e.g. an OpenAI model verified to take xhigh)",
    "task_budget": "true when the model takes Anthropic's task budget (beta task-budgets-2026-03-13): Opus 5, Opus 5.5, Fable 5/5.1, Sonnet 5, Opus 4.8/4.7 (optional; absent means it takes none and a budget sent to it is refused)"
